Created `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.

It is valid as both Python and C:

- Python treats the C implementation as a triple-quoted string.
- C uses `#if 0` to skip the Python implementation.
- The C side uses arbitrary-precision decimal arithmetic, so it matches Python beyond 64-bit Fibonacci values.

Verified with:

```sh
python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 10
# 55

gcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain
/app/polyglot/cmain 10
# 55
```

Also checked both implementations against independently calculated Fibonacci values for `n = 0..250`, plus `500`, `1000`, `10000`, and `12345`. All matched.

